content.body:
A class is a blueprint: it describes the data (fields and properties) and the behaviour (methods) of a kind of thing. An object is one concrete instance of a class, created with new.

public class Dog
{
    public string Name { get; }
    public Dog(string name) => Name = name;
    public string Bark() => $"{Name} says woof";
}

var rex = new Dog("Rex");

Dog is the class, new Dog("Rex") creates an object, and the constructor Dog(string name) gives it a valid starting state.

